# Powers by repeated multiplication in lambda plus merge, with no label:
# scored points where a reverse index of a knowledge base pays (the reverse
# index: one large Scott value read many times).
#
# THE PROGRAM computes base^k by k multiplications, power k = k 1
# (\p. times base (power p)), with the label-free binary times and
# equality of contest_merge_dynamic.pl, and compares it with a claimed
# numeral. The base, one let-bound binary numeral, is an argument of every
# multiplication: a knowledge base that recognizes its meaning once, and
# the catalogued times (merge_binary_times) by its address, can multiply
# natively from then on. The accumulator occurs twice in times's odd case
# and the language is call by name, so without sharing each power is
# evaluated again at every use.
#
# THE TWINS (miss twins) are ALGORITHMIC, measuring a setting's
# fallback: they use the twin arithmetic of contest_merge_dynamic.pl,
# whose times recurses on its right operand, here the growing accumulator,
# and whose plus and equality case on the second operand first; no
# catalogued API and no Böhm-equal respelling of one occurs in them.
#
# THE POINTS: the base 12345678 raised to 4, 8 and 16 (n, 2n and 4n; 16 at
# the edge) and to 32 beyond, each with its twin. The claims are computed
# from Prolog's arithmetic.
#
# READINGS (2026-09-28, CPU 2 under contest_limited.sh, a fresh process per
# reading, the boolean(true) template, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB):
# - weak_head is stopped on every point, the accumulator evaluated again
#   at every use;
# - tabling(weak_head): 4 and 8 in 642 and 2639 ms, 16 at the edge (read in
#   11296 ms of CPU in a probe, stopped at 11683 ms in the points' run), 32
#   stopped; the twins 4, 8 and 16 in 571, 2458 and 11015 ms, 32 stopped.
#   A doubling of the exponent costs about 4, the numbers growing in bits
#   with the exponent.
# LIMITS: the family's, 10 s, 256 MB, 256 MB.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - sharing the accumulator, which call by name evaluates again at every
#   use: J. Launchbury, A Natural Semantics for Lazy Evaluation, POPL 1993,
#   doi:10.1145/158511.158618.
# - recognising the base's meaning and the catalogued times once, then
#   multiplying natively: J.-C. Filliâtre, S. Conchon, Type-Safe Modular
#   Hash-Consing, ML Workshop 2006, doi:10.1145/1159876.1159880.

#   power_point(?Point, ?Arithmetic, ?Exponent)
#
# The arithmetic is a constructor of merge_power/arithmetic, original or
# twin. Each other text is from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of
# bytes, imported from corpora/library/text/cbor. Each number is from_cbor of an
# integer literal, a Scott integer, imported from corpora/library/integer/cbor.
# FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "integer") "cbor")
λ integer_from_cbor _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. integer_from_cbor λx. x)
λ integer
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "merge_power") "arithmetic")
λ original twin
. export
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_four") original λ. integer 4)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_eight") original λ. integer 8)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_sixteen") original λ. integer 16)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_thirty_two") original λ. integer 32)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_four_twin") twin λ. integer 4)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_eight_twin") twin λ. integer 8)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_sixteen_twin") twin λ. integer 16)
λ
. cons (λ_power_point. _power_point (text "merge_power_thirty_two_twin") twin λ. integer 32) nil
